{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"581f45644d92803ae8652802eb862b4a313c03ba3a4d2e7508d07c24e6dd4b6b","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-plan gate and code-reading gates","key_entities":["rebar.llm.gate_source.resolve_gate_handle","rebar.signing._gate_commit_sha","rebar._build_info.COMMIT","hatch_build.py","/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots","verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets","rebar.toml"],"problem_keywords":["gate run","build drift","stale build","commit ancestry","warning detection"],"propositions":["Gate runs do not warn when the executing build's commit is a strict ancestor of the base ref's pinned sha, allowing stale binaries to silently process current config without detecting schema changes.","Config unknown-key warnings are misleading when build drift exists, suggesting 'typo?' rather than indicating the build predates the key's introduction.","A code-reading gate must detect and emit a single warning per (build sha, pinned sha) pair when drift is detected, without failing the run or altering verdict/signature.","The drift check must remain silent when build provenance is unavailable, when the build sha is absent from the target repo, or when the build is at or ahead of the pinned sha."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787587283958311001,"uuid":"f139e5b6-77d0-4fb2-975f-3bd0e0ca8a2f"}